{title: 317 - Lead Me to Calvary}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #317 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Db}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 317}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Db]King of my life, I [Gb]crown Thee [Db]now, Thine shall the glory [Ab]be;
[Db]Lest I forget Thy [Gb]thorn crowned [Db]brow, Lead me to Cal[Ab7]va[Db]ry.
[Ab]Lest I for[Ab7]get Geth[Db]semane, [Ab]Lest I for[Ab7]get Thine [Db]agony;
[Bbm]Lest I for[F7]get Thy [Gb]love for [Db]me, Lead me to Cal[Ab7]va[Db]ry.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Db]Lest [Gb]I [Db]forget [Ab]Gethsemane,
[Db]Lest [Gb]I [Db]forget [Ab7]Thine [Db]agony;
[Ab]Lest [Ab7]I [Db]forget [Ab]Thy [Ab7]love [Db]for me,
[Bbm][F7]Lead [Gb]me [Db][Ab7]to [Db]Calvary.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Db]Show me [Gb]the tomb [Db]where Thou [Ab]wast laid,
[Db][Gb]Tenderly [Db]mourned [Ab7]and [Db]wept;
[Ab]Angels [Ab7]in [Db]robes [Ab]of [Ab7]light [Db]arrayed
[Bbm][F7]Guarded [Gb]Thee [Db]whilst [Ab7]Thou [Db]slept.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Db]Let [Gb]me like [Db]Mary, through [Ab]the gloom,
[Db]Come [Gb]with [Db]a [Ab7]gift [Db]to Thee;
[Ab]Show [Ab7]to [Db]me [Ab]now [Ab7]the [Db]empty tomb,
[Bbm][F7]Lead [Gb]me [Db][Ab7]to [Db]Calvary.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Db]May [Gb]I be [Db]willing, Lord, [Ab]to bear
[Db]Daily [Gb]my [Db]cross [Ab7]for [Db]Thee;
[Ab]Even [Ab7]Thy [Db]cup [Ab]of [Ab7]grief [Db]to share,
[Bbm]Thou [F7]hast [Gb]borne [Db]all [Ab7]for [Db]me.
{end_of_verse}
